    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To implement the extract_receipt_fields.py file, I need to use a concrete external provider for extracting fields from a receipt. I will use the Amazon Textract service, which is a machine learning service that automatically extracts text, handwriting, and data from scanned documents. I will make the provider identifiable in the code by importing the boto3 library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python, and by using the specific Textract client and API calls. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789864220292,
          "start": 1789864216637
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc38883d001AxRYF9ta5wz9Wv",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc388447001IdioRTLSaXRvPj",
